---
description: "Iteratively fix Rust compiler errors one at a time"
globs: ["**/*.rs"]
alwaysApply: false
---

When working with Rust files:

- Run `cargo build` to compile the project.
- If there are compiler errors, identify the first error reported.
- Navigate to the source code location of the first error.
- Apply the minimal change necessary to fix this error.
- Do not make changes unrelated to the current error.
- Save the file after applying the fix.
- Re-run `cargo build` to check for remaining errors.
- Repeat this process until `cargo build` completes successfully without errors.
